      "message": "I decoded the `X509_LICENSE_FILE_CERTIFICATE_SIGNED_BY_ANOTHER_CA` certificate.\n\n```\nopenssl x509 -in certificate.pem -text -noout\n```\n\nIt looks like it does not contain a SAN extension?\n\n```\nX509v3 extensions:\n            X509v3 Basic Constraints:\n                CA:FALSE\n            Netscape Comment:\n                OpenSSL Generated Certificate\n            X509v3 Subject Key Identifier:\n                35:2F:E6:CC:53:13:75:52:A2:33:6E:33:01:6E:71:BC:AC:77:E4:48\n            X509v3 Authority Key Identifier:\n                50:C9:69:B2:54:78:25:10:26:6E:29:89:45:BD:10:5D:4F:25:3E:F2\n```\n\nIt does not have:\n\n```\n            X509v3 Subject Alternative Name:\n                DNS:gerrit-bsl-license\n```\n\nIn that case, it wouldn\u0027t license the installed plugin even if its CA were trusted, right?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 286,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 286,
        "endChar": 82
